1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
An air handler starts drifting in a critical building.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,000
The alarm is easy. The hard question is what

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,000
failed, which instructions are safe, and who can reach

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
it before the service window closes.

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,050
Sensor trends sit in one system. Equipment manuals sit

6
00:00:15,050 --> 00:00:18,100
in another. Dispatch rules live in spreadsheets and experience.

7
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:21,150
Each handoff creates another place for evidence or time

8
00:00:21,150 --> 00:00:24,200
to disappear.

9
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:28,700
Uptime Desk joins that path on AWS. Recorded LBNL

10
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:33,200
data streams through Kinesis. Rules stay primary while XGBoost

11
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:37,700
supplies a second opinion. Bedrock proposes a diagnosis from

12
00:00:37,700 --> 00:00:42,200
manual pages, then a second model verifies each quotation.

13
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:46,700
PostgreSQL rejects unverified steps. Step Functions waits for a

14
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:51,200
manager, then OR-Tools assigns a qualified technician. Cognito and

15
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:55,700
the MCP gateway bind requests to a verified identity.

16
00:00:55,700 --> 00:00:59,567
The manager launches a recorded field scenario and watches

17
00:00:59,567 --> 00:01:03,433
each stage complete. The diagnosis shows rules, model, and

18
00:01:03,433 --> 00:01:07,300
disagreement. Every accepted check opens the source manual at

19
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:11,167
the cited page. The manager keeps control: approve the

20
00:01:11,167 --> 00:01:15,033
draft, remove an optional step, or reject it with

21
00:01:15,033 --> 00:01:18,900
a reason. Approval resumes the case machine. The dispatch

22
00:01:18,900 --> 00:01:22,767
board shows the selected technician, a runner-up, travel, lateness,

23
00:01:22,767 --> 00:01:26,633
and rationale. The assistant can list that technician's jobs

24
00:01:26,633 --> 00:01:30,500
and answer from verified passages. A request for another

25
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:34,367
technician's order is denied and audited. A passing hosted

26
00:01:34,367 --> 00:01:38,233
run reached a draft in a median 39.4 seconds

27
00:01:38,233 --> 00:01:42,100
and dispatch in 77.3. If the case has no

28
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:45,967
sourced lockout step, the pipeline stops. In the hosted

29
00:01:45,967 --> 00:01:49,833
batch, that policy blocked 2 of 10 runs instead

30
00:01:49,833 --> 00:01:53,700
of sending unsupported work.

31
00:01:53,700 --> 00:01:58,400
The measured results keep their boundaries. On lab air

32
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:03,100
handlers, model recall was 0.957 against 0.739 for rules.

33
00:02:03,100 --> 00:02:07,800
Rules won on the lab economizer and field RTU.

34
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:12,500
Citation support was 0.880 against 0.122. In the dispatch

35
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:17,200
scenario, OR-Tools cut lateness from 1,343 to 402 minutes

36
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:21,900
against nearest qualified, while earliest available also reached 402.

